        "4. Fixed Bias Configuration: Stability factor is S_fixed = β + 1 = 120 + 1 = 121. Total increase in collector current due to leakage: ΔI_C = S_fixed · ΔI_CBO = 121 × (480 nA - 15 nA) = 121 × 465 nA = 56.27 μA. (For low-current preamps biased at 100 μA, this represents a devastating 56% operating point shift!).",
        "5. Voltage Divider Bias Configuration with R_E = 1.0 kΩ, R_TH = 3.3 kΩ: Stability factor formula: S_VDB = (1 + β) / [ 1 + (β · R_E) / (R_TH + R_E) ] = 121 / [ 1 + (120 × 1000) / (3300 + 1000) ] = 121 / [ 1 + 120000 / 4300 ] = 121 / [ 1 + 27.91 ] = 121 / 28.91 = 4.18.",
